      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I was going to add some discussion in b/266879860 about this, as I was\nworking through the options, but didn\u0027t get around to completely capturing\nwhat I wanted to say.\nThe issue is that there are assumptions about the debug level and\nwhether the labels are stored, so that it is not possible to set an initial\ndebug level of 0 (to prevent excess logging), allow this to be modified via\nthe CLI, and not have the labels present (so that the state numbers are\nused instead).\nIt would be good to have a separate config item to specify whether the\nlabels are present, and then to have a separate init debug level. In this\ncase I am not sure that the FIXED_DEBUG_LEVEL is required (which doesn\u0027t seem\nthat useful in that the only useful setting is 0 to stop all logging and not\nstore the labels).\nI\u0027ve now copied this bit into that bug.\n\nSo I think more work is needed to clean this up a bit, and in the meantime,\nmaybe I\u0027ll just stick with the CONFIG_SHELL_HELP\u003dn which likely\ngives us enough head room for the short term.",
